  "xlogValidationDesign": {
    "authority": "proposed xLog validation policy, not an official SST rule",
    "officialBoundary": "The sponsor says each QSO earns one point; xLog must not retain an accepted QSO and silently turn it into a zero-point nonduplicate.",
    "draftCommit": "A draft with unresolved or contradictory geography cannot be committed, so it never becomes a QSO, earns no point or multiplier, and occupies no duplicate key.",
    "retainedContact": "An accepted contact keeps its immutable resolved entity and reference-data version. Later reference drift cannot delete or reclassify it silently; replay scores the pinned snapshot. Corrupt retained data is a surfaced session validation failure requiring correction, not an implicit zero-point QSO."
  },
